WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.994
Color and Post FX change how the beam looks on screen, after the scan processor has drawn it.

2
00:00:06.457 --> 00:00:08.230
Color Mode picks the phosphor.

3
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.885
Amber, like an old terminal.

4
00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:11.008
Then back to green.

5
00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:13.067
Bloom is the phosphor glow.

6
00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:15.737
Push the intensity for a hot, blown-out beam.

7
00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:18.960
Burn-In Feedback leaves trails, like slow phosphor.

8
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.347
Turn it on, and move the camera to see them.

9
00:00:24.593 --> 00:00:27.983
In Virtual Camera, Field of View works like a zoom lens.

10
00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:39.866
Presets apply a whole look at once.

11
00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:40.776
Heavy Bloom.

12
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:41.988
Lissajous Scope.

13
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:42.973
Classic 1974.

14
00:00:48.335 --> 00:00:52.417
Mix and match, then save your own look in the Presets section.

15
00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:53.536
Next: modulation.
